cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Another Take (CS): the bench-bedside nanomedicine programme as a verified dataflow program"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Adya
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-10-23
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A computer-science reframing of a dual-loop biological intervention world
  model. The multiscale delivery chain is treated as a verified dataflow program
  over typed biological quantities, separating claims that are properties of the
  program -- true by construction and checkable before any data -- from claims
  that require experimental evidence. Mass conservation is an algebraic identity
  of a Metzler zero-column-sum generator rather than a fitted property;
  compositional corona shares lie on the simplex by construction; provenance
  propagates as an information-flow lattice in which no operation lowers a
  taint; uncertainty obeys a monotonicity invariant so a composition can never be
  more certain than its inputs; and the organ-to-cytosol handoff is shown to be
  structurally unidentifiable from whole-organ measurement, with the minimal
  additional assays that would close it returned automatically. A credibility
  gate reads taint and identifiability rather than a declared maturity label, and
  refuses every patient-facing context of use by construction.
keywords:
  - nanomedicine
  - multiscale modelling
  - structural identifiability
  - information flow
  - uncertainty propagation
  - conformal prediction
  - empirical Bayes
  - model credibility
